signalmeow (mautrix-signal's pkg/signalmeow at 01626c1) pointed at a Signal-Server test box.

Its hosts, TLS roots, gRPC target, zkgroup server public parameters and unidentified-sender
trust roots are compiled in (pkg/signalmeow/web/web.go, grpc.go, misc.go, and
pkg/libsignalgo/sendercertificate.go). The hosts and the gRPC target become variables, and
web/box.go reads the box's /keys/desktop-config.json, which SIGNALMEOW_BOX_CONFIG names, in
init(): the hosts with their ports, the box's CA as the only TLS root, its zkgroup parameters and
its trust roots. Without the variable nothing changes.

Chat is signalmeow's own websocket and gRPC, not libsignal-net, so libsignal needs no patch
(unlike Signal-Android's: testbox/patches/libsignal-local.patch).

